    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Following the consolidation of airlines in the United States in the past fifteen years, the decrease in competition has created room for new players in markets traditionally dominated by legacy carriers like American, Delta, and United. While ultra-low-cost carriers (ULCC) have thrived in regions like Europe and Southeast Asia, the ultra-low-cost model is still developing, albeit at an extremely rapid pace, in the United States. In this paper, I employ a difference-in-differences approach on markets that have experienced the new entry of a ULCC from 2013 to 2017. I estimate the effect of ULCC entry on incumbent carrier airfares as a whole, as well as how individual incumbent carriers responded differently to new ULCC entry. Additionally, I also examine whether the response differed based on the entering ULCC.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
